# LF in the working tree, on every platform.
#
# Prettier's `endOfLine` defaults to "lf", and `format:check` is the FIRST step
# of `scripts/gate.mjs`. Without this file a clone on a Windows machine with the
# default `core.autocrlf=true` checks out CRLF and fails that step on every file
# in the repo — 248 of them on 2026-08-23, on a clone whose tree was byte-clean
# against HEAD. The repair looks like `prettier --write .`, which rewrites the
# whole repo into a diff that hides whatever was actually being worked on.
#
# `text=auto` so git still keeps binaries out of it; `eol=lf` so the checkout
# matches what the gate demands rather than what the platform prefers.
#
# THE FAILURE IS WORSE THAN THE GATE STEP THAT FOUND IT. Diagnosed on branch
# `claude/windows-clone-lf-and-cli-override`, 2026-08-21, four days before this
# file landed and independently of it: Vite's shebang strip matches `#!...\n`
# only, so `scripts/*.mjs` checked out as `#!/usr/bin/env node\r\n` have the
# injected CJS import prepended onto the shebang's own line and rolldown stops at
# ``Invalid Character `!` ``. **23 test files failed to PARSE**, every one naming
# a script it imports rather than anything it asserts. `format:check` is simply
# the first step that notices; it is not the extent of the damage.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Decks and images are bytes. Normalising them corrupts them.
#
# `text=auto` above already applies to these — `git check-attr` reports
# `text: auto` on `examples/showcase.pptx` — so today they are protected by git's
# binary HEURISTIC rather than by anything anyone wrote down. The heuristic is
# good and these files are full of NUL bytes, so it holds. It is still a guess
# standing in for a declaration, on the two artifacts `verify-deck` and
# `validate-ooxml` run against.
*.pptx binary
*.png binary
